title: Visual novels
intro: A stage with backgrounds and characters, directed by the lines of a dialogue: who's on, where they stand, how they look, and who's speaking.
project: Empty | Park Story

chapter: A stage | Entity > Genres > Visual Novels > Stage
create: Stage
expectcount: Ava = 1
expectcount: Ben = 1
expectcount: Dialogue Box = 1
explain: component:Stage | Stage | A stage shows a background and the characters inside it, standing at named positions: left, center and right, or your own.
explain: field:Stage.Backgrounds | Backgrounds | Its backgrounds are pictures, here a park and a room, or plain colors.
select: Ava
explain: component:Character | Character | Ava is a character with three expressions, each a picture. An expression can be an animation clip as well.
select: Stage
explain: field:Dialogue.Lines | Directed by its lines | The stage's dialogue directs it. Tags on a line show, hide and move characters and change the background, and a line can say how its speaker looks as they say it.

chapter: Editing lines | Entity > Edit Dialogue
menu: Entity > Edit Dialogue...
dialogue
dialogueline: 2
explain: dialogue:preview | The stage at a line | The Dialogue Editor lists the lines and shows the stage as the line picked leaves it. Nobody's on stage yet for the narrator's first line.
dialogueset: kind = Show
dialogueset: who = Ava
dialogueset: position = Left
dialogueset: face = Neutral
dialogueset: transition = fade
click: dialogue:adddirection
expectpreview: Park. Ava at Left, Neutral
explain: dialogue:directions | Picked from lists | Directions are picked from what the stage has: its characters, positions, expressions and backgrounds. Now Ava fades in as the narrator speaks.
dialogueline: 5
dialogueset: expression = Sad
expectpreview: Ava at Left, Sad, speaking; Ben at Right, Surprised, dimmed
explain: dialogue:preview | Who's speaking | Ava says this line looking sad. Whoever speaks is lit, and the others on stage are dimmed.
click: dialogue:close

chapter: Reading it | Click, tap, or press Space
play
wait: 2
expectvalue: Ava.Character.Expression = Neutral
explain: game | Read on | The script starts by itself. A click or a tap anywhere, Space, Enter or a gamepad button reads on, finishing the line being typed first.
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 2
expectvalue: Ava.Character.Expression = Happy
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 2
expectvalue: Stage.Dialogue.Line = 3
say: Ben slides in from the right.
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 2
expectvalue: Ava.Character.Expression = Sad
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 2
gameclick: 0, 3
wait: 2
expectvalue: Stage.Dialogue.Line = 6
say: A choice. Two goes home for tea.
wait: 2
tap: D2
wait: 2
expectvalue: Stage.Stage.Background = Room
explain: game | A new scene | The background fades to the room, Ben leaves and Ava walks to the middle.
stop
say: That's visual novel scenes: backgrounds and characters with positions and expressions, all directed from the lines of a dialogue, and saved with the scene, so rewinding goes back into the middle of a talk.
